        },
        {
          "text": "**Vector Databases & Embeddings:** A technical dive into the *storage mechanism* that makes RAG possible. How is text converted into mathematical vectors, and how do databases search these vectors for semantic relevance?",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 103,
          "source": "topic-set-the-principles-and-applications-of-context-engineering-🆔20251021214416.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Transformer \"Attention\" Mechanisms:** An exploration of the *architectural reason* context matters. How does the \"attention\" layer in a transformer model decide which tokens in the context window are most important?",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 108,
          "source": "topic-set-the-principles-and-applications-of-context-engineering-🆔20251021214416.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Context-Aware Fine-Tuning:** The next step after Context Engineering. How can models be permanently trained (fine-tuned) on specific datasets to make their \"knowledge\" part of their internal parameters rather than requiring it in the context window every time?",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 111,
          "source": "topic-set-the-principles-and-applications-of-context-engineering-🆔20251021214416.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Agentic Architectures (e.g., ReAct):** Investigating frameworks where LLMs autonomously decide when to *reason* and when to *act* (i.e., call a tool), creating a loop of thought, action, and observation that constantly re-engineers its own context.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 119,
          "source": "topic-set-the-principles-and-applications-of-context-engineering-🆔20251021214416.md"
        }
      ]
